A||||1||btoth||Couple parking break ?'s||||1||
Z||000000||btoth||05-31-2001||02:49 PM||||1.)  When you release the break, is the button supposed to be in or out? (Dumb question, I know.)<P>2.)  If I hit a bump, sometimes the break lever bounces up just high enough to have the button come out and it sets off the light and warning signal.... is there a way to tighten the handle down so this won't happen?||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-31-2001||02:53 PM||||To release, lift the handle until you overcome the cable tension, press the button and hold while lowering the handle.<P>You may need to adjust your parking brake cable. The only thing that provides tension against the warning light switch is a properly adjusted cable.<P>I sure hope this question didn't result from you pulling the brake handle beyond the last ratchet spot due to a loose cable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">. If you did that and your EB lever is old and loose enough, it may not disengage properly. If so, you will have to pull the sill (cover) off and use a screwdriver to release the cable prior to adjusting it up.<P>I got to learn all this first hand last weekend when I fixed mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
